# Both functions have left for unseen code, so nothing is proven of `step`. What the calls that are written in the function's own file hand over is text of that file: a function written at the call, or an
# element of a list of functions written in the caller: those are expected: in front of a loop that calls the parameter a test for each, and a build of the loop for each where that pays. It is an expectation and no proof: who else comes
# (a function out of the module's own body, a built-in) fails the test and is called as any value. No type of the rest of the program is read for it, and no call of another file.
